.SS polymorph capture
Run the discovery procedure against a harness, headless, in a scratch directory.
.PP
.nf
polymorph capture [\-\-harness HARNESS] [\-\-yes] [\-\-keep] [\-\-steps STEP] [\-\-step\-timeout SECONDS] [\-\-total\-timeout SECONDS] [\-\-out DIR] [\-\-print\-prompts] [\-\-full] [\-\-i\-really\-want\-this\-in\-the\-repo\-raw]
.fi
.TP
.B \-\-harness HARNESS
driver name (see below); required unless \-\-print\-prompts
.TP
.B \-\-yes
skip the typed confirmation (required when stdin is not a terminal)
.TP
.B \-\-keep
keep the scratch directory afterwards
.TP
.B \-\-steps STEP
run only these steps, in the fixed order: shell, file, search, background
.TP
.B \-\-step\-timeout SECONDS
kill a step after this many seconds (default 120.0)
.TP
.B \-\-total\-timeout SECONDS
skip the remaining steps after this many seconds (default 600.0)
.TP
.B \-\-out DIR
results directory (default ./polymorph\-capture\-NAME; must be absent or empty)
.TP
.B \-\-print\-prompts
print the prompt kit for a harness with no driver, run nothing, exit 0
.TP
.B \-\-full
log raw payloads (commands, paths, contents); default is redacted. Needs \-\-out and the long flag below, then asks you to type yes
.TP
.B \-\-i\-really\-want\-this\-in\-the\-repo\-raw
required with \-\-full: accept a plain\-text raw log (then type yes when asked)
.SS polymorph discover
Log a harness's hook payloads and draft a mapping.
.PP
